  "notes": "Specifically refers to physical growth and development of the body, especially of children, infants, and organisms. Composed of {発|はつ} (emit, develop) and {育|いく} (grow, raise). Primarily used in medical, childcare, and biological contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {発育|はついく}が{良|よ}い/{悪|わる}い: good/poor development\n- {発育|はついく}{状態|じょうたい}: growth condition\n- {発育|はついく}{不良|ふりょう}: poor growth, failure to thrive\n- {発育|はついく}{段階|だんかい}: stage of development\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {成長|せいちょう}: growth — broader; includes physical, mental, and figurative growth\n- {発達|はったつ}: development — emphasizes functional and mental development\n- {生育|せいいく}: growth — used for plants and organisms in natural environments",
